<%
def url(page, params = nil)
  @base_url + "?page=" + page + (params ? "&#{params}" : "")
end

def time(t)
  return '---' unless t

  local_time(t, '%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S')
end

def value(v)
  v.nil? || v.to_s.empty? ? '---' : v
end

zone = @object
states_by_primary = zone.alert_eligible_primary_transfer_states.group_by(&:dns_zone_transfer)
-%>
Hi <%= @user.login %>,

transfer-readiness checks and BIND transfer diagnostics show that one or more
of our secondary DNS servers cannot obtain and validate DNS zone
<%= zone.name %> directly from your configured primary DNS servers.

Affected direct synchronization paths:
<% states_by_primary.each do |transfer, states| -%>

Primary server: <%= transfer.ip_addr %>
<% states.each do |state| -%>
- Secondary server: <%= state.dns_server_zone.dns_server.name %> (<%= state.secondary_source_addr %>)
  Failure detected: <%= time(state.failed_since) %>
  Error code: <%= value(state.reason_code) %>
  Reason: <%= value(state.reason) %>
<% end -%>
  Transfer logs:
  <%= url('dns', "action=transfer_log&dns_zone=#{zone.id}&dns_zone_transfer=#{transfer.id}") %>
<% end -%>

This does not necessarily mean that the zone is unavailable. Another secondary
server may have supplied a current copy. The failed readiness paths can,
however, prevent future updates from reaching all secondary servers reliably.

Please check that the primary servers are reachable, serve a valid zone, use
the configured TSIG authentication, and allow AXFR/IXFR transfers from the
affected secondary server addresses.

If you acknowledge this issue, you will not receive more alerts until it is
detected again after being resolved:

  <%= url('monitoring', "action=ack&id=#{@event.id}") %>

Best regards,

vpsFree.cz team

(This is an automated mail from vpsAdmin, your reply will be sent to our support)
